From f1a606023b241d75885bbcb759074c46884b7b84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 05:45:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 122/250] perf(pypto-x): add AVX-512 packed/blocked matmul (W8B
 avx512-blocked-gemm)

Implement the packed/blocked rank-2 matmul plane for long-standing Qwen3.5
dense-linear shapes on cpu.avx512:

- K64 x N64 tile layout, k-pair interleaved bf16, four ZMM column
  accumulators, bounded pthread workers (<= 6), and bitwise-preserving k
  order so the packed result is byte-identical to the shipped column-block
  kernel for f32 and bf16.
- Parameter-chain dispatch: a rank-2 matmul whose right operand is a cast/
  transpose/identity chain rooted in one function parameter is packed once
  and executed by ptx_avx512_matmul_packed_{f32,bf16,bf16_f32}; every other
  rank-2 matmul stays on native_avx512_zmm and is enumerated with a reason in
  matmul_legacy_operations (no silent fallback).
- The runtime recomputes the dispatch from the immutable program with the
  same predicate that writes the artifact metadata; a declared parameter that
  is unavailable fails closed.
- Opt-in cross-launch packed-weight cache (PYPTO_X_AVX512_WEIGHT_CACHE) with
  sampled-fingerprint invalidation and a 2 GiB byte bound; default is
  per-launch packing.
- Bounded thread count via PYPTO_X_AVX512_GEMM_THREADS (1..6, invalid values
  fail loud); batched rank-4 matmul now walks pointer offsets instead of
  materializing Python element lists per batch.

Artifact contract: payload 3 -> 4, native ABI marker 4 -> 5; old artifacts
are rejected before load and tampered packed dispatch metadata fails the
metadata recomputation check. Numerics are unchanged (bit-identical).

New focused tests cover f32/bf16/mixed parameter chains, K/N/M tails,
bitwise equality against the legacy kernel, bounded threads, the opt-in
cache, metadata tampering, and the 187 packed plans of the real decoder
graph.
